  m_text: The pages of House & Garden are full of beautiful textiles, both modern
    and antique, drawn from a vast variety of traditions around the world. The traditions
    of the Indian subcontinent alone have been immeasurably influential on English
    decoration; the lively, colourful floral patterns of chintz, for example, have
    never left us since their arrival in the eighteenth century
