      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'In the Indian subcontinent, one of the earliest available Bronze age swords
    of copper was discovered by the period of Indus Valley civilization. Swords have
    been recovered in archaeological findings throughout the Ganges-Jamuna Doab region
    of Indian subcontinent, consisting of bronze but more commonly copper. Swords
    have been also discovered in Fatehgarh, where there are several varieties of
    hilt. These swords have been variously dated to times between 1700 and 1400 BC. '
